1
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [grunts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,066
-This is my little brother George.
-[grunting]

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:10,299
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[grunts]

4
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:13,033
-And this is Daddy Pig.
-[grunts]

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,166
[laugh]

6
00:00:14,233 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [grunts]

7
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,366
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:20,200
[narrator] It is playtime at school.

9
00:00:20,266 --> 00:00:23,466
Peppa and her friends
are running around, having fun.

10
00:00:23,599 --> 00:00:26,066
Ow! That hurts.

11
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:28,133
Are you all right, Peppa?

12
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,266
I've hurt my knee.

13
00:00:30,333 --> 00:00:34,233
[squeaks] Madame Gazelle,
Peppa has fallen over.

14
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,500
You've just grazed your knee, Peppa.

15
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:40,633
First Madame Gazelle cleans Peppa's knee.

16
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,333
Then she puts a plaster on it.

17
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:46,300
-Does that feel any better?
-Yes. Thank you.

18
00:00:46,366 --> 00:00:51,400
Now, children, you may have noticed
that Pedro Pony isn't here today.

19
00:00:51,466 --> 00:00:53,133
Is he late again?

20
00:00:53,199 --> 00:00:56,300
No, Suzy. Pedro is in hospital.

21
00:00:56,366 --> 00:00:57,266
[in unison] Ooh.

22
00:00:57,333 --> 00:00:59,733
And today we are going to visit him.

23
00:01:01,699 --> 00:01:03,466
This is the hospital.

24
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:06,633
Peppa and her friends have come
to visit Pedro Pony.

25
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:11,266
Remember, children, stay close to me.
I don't want you getting lost.

26
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:13,200
[in unison] Yes, Madame Gazelle.

27
00:01:13,266 --> 00:01:17,800
Excuse me, Mr. Bull,
which way is the children's ward?

28
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:19,666
Down the steps, double doors,

29
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:24,300
right, left, right, along the corridor,
up the stairs, third on your left.

30
00:01:24,366 --> 00:01:26,733
-Ah.
-Or you could just take the lift.

31
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,166
[laughing]

32
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,766
[Mr. Bull] Children's ward.

33
00:01:34,366 --> 00:01:40,000
[bleats] Pedro will be asleep.
Sick people do a lot of sleeping.

34
00:01:40,066 --> 00:01:41,533
Hello, everyone.

35
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,333
[in unison] Hello, Pedro.

36
00:01:43,399 --> 00:01:46,533
Why aren't you asleep?
You don't look sick.

37
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:51,766
I broke my leg,
and they put it in this plaster cast.

38
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:52,733
[all] Wow!

39
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,800
The plaster cast helps
Pedro's leg get better.

40
00:01:56,033 --> 00:02:00,199
I grazed my knee,
and I got a plaster, too.

41
00:02:00,266 --> 00:02:01,466
Wow.

42
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:04,766
Do you want to draw on my plaster cast?

43
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,300
Yes, please.

44
00:02:06,366 --> 00:02:10,233
The children are all doing drawings
on Pedro's plaster cast.

45
00:02:10,433 --> 00:02:13,000
[Danny] I'm drawing a football.

46
00:02:13,066 --> 00:02:15,166
[Emily] I've drawn some flowers.

47
00:02:15,233 --> 00:02:16,733
[Rebecca] Mr. Potato.

48
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:18,033
[Suzy] A parrot.

49
00:02:18,466 --> 00:02:21,666
[Peppa] And I've drawn a muddy puddle.

50
00:02:21,733 --> 00:02:24,633
Wow, thanks, everyone.

51
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:27,533
You can draw on my plaster, too.

52
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,466
Okay. I'll draw a little flower.

53
00:02:30,533 --> 00:02:32,500
Thank you, Pedro.

54
00:02:32,566 --> 00:02:36,000
Pedro, what's it like being in hospital?

55
00:02:36,066 --> 00:02:37,266
It's great.

56
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:39,166
[whispers] What are the nurses like?

57
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:41,266
They give me stickers.

58
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:42,333
[all] Wow.

59
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:46,266
And they come
whenever I press this button.

60
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:47,666
[buzzes]

61
00:02:47,733 --> 00:02:50,066
Who's that? I wonder.

62
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:51,766
Could it be Pedro?

63
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,633
What do you want, Pedro? We are very busy.

64
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,066
I've got a bit of an itch.

65
00:02:58,133 --> 00:03:00,366
Even if your leg is itching,

66
00:03:00,433 --> 00:03:04,666
we can't take the cast off
until your leg is better.

67
00:03:04,733 --> 00:03:09,133
It's not my leg that's itching.
It's my ear.

68
00:03:10,166 --> 00:03:11,433
Is that better?

69
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,733
Yes, thank you. [giggles]

70
00:03:13,799 --> 00:03:17,700
Lunchtime.
What would you like to eat today, Pedro?

71
00:03:17,766 --> 00:03:21,533
Can I have spaghetti
and sponge pudding, please?

72
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,799
You get your dinner in bed?

73
00:03:24,033 --> 00:03:26,266
Yes. [giggles]

74
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:28,566
Mm. That looks tasty.

75
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:32,200
Dr. Brown Bear has come
to see how Pedro is doing.

76
00:03:32,266 --> 00:03:34,200
How are we today, Pedro?

77
00:03:34,266 --> 00:03:38,166
My ear is a bit itchy, just here.

78
00:03:39,566 --> 00:03:43,566
Mm. I'd say you're almost better.

79
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:44,700
[giggles]

80
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,133
[dings]

81
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,133
Visiting time is over.

82
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,466
[in unison] Bye, Pedro.

83
00:03:49,533 --> 00:03:51,066
Bye, everyone.

84
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:52,666
Get well soon, Pedro.

85
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:54,433
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

86
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,333
[clamoring]

87
00:03:56,399 --> 00:03:58,033
It is another school day.

88
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,200
Peppa and her friends are playing
in the playground.

89
00:04:01,266 --> 00:04:06,666
Madame Gazelle, my plaster has fallen off.
Can I have another one?

90
00:04:06,733 --> 00:04:11,166
You don't need a plaster, Peppa.
Your knee is better.

91
00:04:11,233 --> 00:04:13,266
Oh, yes. [giggles]

92
00:04:14,166 --> 00:04:15,566
Hello, everyone.

93
00:04:15,633 --> 00:04:17,300
Pedro Pony is back.

94
00:04:17,366 --> 00:04:19,633
Oh, hello, Pedro.

95
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,800
Where's your plaster cast?

96
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:25,466
They took it off because my leg is better.

97
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:27,733
Is your leg stronger now?

98
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:33,133
It's stronger than it was before.
It's a super leg.

99
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,700
Can you run on it?

100
00:04:34,766 --> 00:04:36,333
Watch this.

101
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,133
[neighs and giggles]

102
00:04:38,599 --> 00:04:41,099
Pedro likes running around, having fun.

103
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:45,133
Everybody likes running around,
having fun.

104
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,566
[all giggling]

105
00:04:48,633 --> 00:04:50,099
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

106
00:04:50,166 --> 00:04:51,633
[narrator] It is springtime.

107
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:54,733
Grandpa Pig has made a chocolate egg hunt.

108
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,800
Is everybody ready?

109
00:04:57,033 --> 00:05:00,433
No, Grandpa. Freddy Fox isn't here.

110
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,599
[horn honks]

111
00:05:02,533 --> 00:05:04,466
[barks] Hello, everyone.

112
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:06,200
Hello, Freddy.

113
00:05:06,266 --> 00:05:10,466
Ah. Hello, Mr. Fox. Are you staying?

114
00:05:10,533 --> 00:05:11,766
I wish I could.

115
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,733
I loved egg hunts when I was a little lad.

116
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,633
-See you later, Freddy.
-[barks]

117
00:05:17,266 --> 00:05:19,766
Now, are we ready for the egg hunt?

118
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,533
[in unison] Yes, Grandpa Pig.

119
00:05:22,599 --> 00:05:27,066
There are lots of chocolate eggs hidden
in my garden.

120
00:05:27,133 --> 00:05:29,099
You must find them.

121
00:05:29,166 --> 00:05:30,333
Easy.

122
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:34,400
[grunts] But be careful not
to step on my little plants.

123
00:05:34,466 --> 00:05:40,400
Oh, it's so exciting in springtime
to see these baby plants starting to grow.

124
00:05:40,466 --> 00:05:43,400
We promise to be careful, Grandpa.

125
00:05:43,466 --> 00:05:46,500
Very good. Off you go, then.

126
00:05:46,766 --> 00:05:48,533
[giggling]

127
00:05:48,599 --> 00:05:51,766
Grandpa Pig's
chocolate egg hunt has begun.

128
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,733
Have you got time for a cup of tea,
Grandpa Pig?

129
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,400
Ho, ho, yes.

130
00:05:56,466 --> 00:06:00,400
It will take them ages to find my eggs.

131
00:06:00,466 --> 00:06:02,533
I've hidden them very well.

132
00:06:02,599 --> 00:06:04,300
Here's an egg. [grunts]

133
00:06:04,366 --> 00:06:07,800
Peppa has found a chocolate egg
in a plant pot.

134
00:06:08,033 --> 00:06:10,333
Here's another egg. [squeaks]

135
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:15,066
Rebecca Rabbit has found a chocolate egg
hiding under a leafy bush.

136
00:06:15,133 --> 00:06:18,599
Hooray, an egg for me. [trumpets]

137
00:06:18,666 --> 00:06:23,266
Emily Elephant has found a chocolate egg
in the branches of a tree.

138
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:24,233
[sniffs]

139
00:06:24,299 --> 00:06:27,433
I think I can smell chocolate.

140
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:30,599
Freddy Fox has a very good sense of smell.

141
00:06:30,666 --> 00:06:32,033
Yes.

142
00:06:32,099 --> 00:06:36,299
Freddy Fox has found a chocolate egg
in the middle of the birdbath.

143
00:06:36,366 --> 00:06:38,266
[giggling]

144
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:42,066
Grandpa, Grandpa.
We found the chocolate eggs.

145
00:06:42,133 --> 00:06:46,000
-It was really fun.
-But it was a bit easy.

146
00:06:46,066 --> 00:06:48,633
It wasn't easy for the little ones.

147
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:54,666
George, Richard, and Edmond
haven't found any eggs.

148
00:06:55,533 --> 00:06:57,233
[crying]

149
00:06:57,299 --> 00:07:00,099
I wonder where the other eggs are.

150
00:07:00,166 --> 00:07:01,633
-Ho-ho-ho!
-[grunts]

151
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,133
Chocky egg.

152
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,099
-Ha-ha-ha!
-[squeaks]

153
00:07:05,166 --> 00:07:07,133
-[giggles]
-Ah.

154
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:11,799
Edmond, I think
there's something behind your ear.

155
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:14,400
[trumpets and giggles]

156
00:07:14,466 --> 00:07:17,366
-Everyone has found a chocolate egg.
-[giggling]

157
00:07:17,433 --> 00:07:20,500
[squeaks] What do we do now, Grandpa Pig?

158
00:07:20,566 --> 00:07:23,666
Ha, ha! You eat them, of course.

159
00:07:27,066 --> 00:07:29,366
-Hello, children.
-Granny, Granny.

160
00:07:29,433 --> 00:07:31,599
We found all the chocolate eggs.

161
00:07:31,666 --> 00:07:34,466
Well, where are they?
I can't see any eggs.

162
00:07:34,533 --> 00:07:37,233
-[chuckles]
-They're in our tummies.

163
00:07:37,299 --> 00:07:38,766
[Granny Pig] And 'round your mouths.

164
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,033
[all laugh]

165
00:07:43,099 --> 00:07:45,233
Did Grandpa hide the eggs well?

166
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:48,566
No. We big ones found them easily.

167
00:07:48,633 --> 00:07:51,799
But the little ones needed helping.

168
00:07:52,033 --> 00:07:53,299
[all sigh]

169
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:58,500
George, Richard, and Edmond
don't like to be the littlest ones.

170
00:07:58,566 --> 00:07:59,633
Don't worry.

171
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:02,366
There'll soon be even littler ones
in the garden.

172
00:08:02,433 --> 00:08:08,566
[grunts] Oh, yes. The little babies.
It's so exciting.

173
00:08:08,633 --> 00:08:13,533
Grandpa already told us
about the baby plants, Granny.

174
00:08:13,599 --> 00:08:15,533
But it's not that exciting.

175
00:08:15,599 --> 00:08:18,566
We're not talking about baby plants,
Peppa.

176
00:08:18,633 --> 00:08:21,266
Oh. What are you talking about?

177
00:08:21,333 --> 00:08:25,666
Let's go and see Jemima,
Vanessa, Sarah, and Neville.

178
00:08:25,733 --> 00:08:27,466
They're chickens.

179
00:08:27,533 --> 00:08:30,333
Yes, and they have eggs, too.

180
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,000
Can we eat them?

181
00:08:32,066 --> 00:08:35,566
No, Freddy. These eggs are about to hatch.

182
00:08:36,033 --> 00:08:38,233
[clucking]

183
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:40,733
Oh! We're just in time.

184
00:08:42,333 --> 00:08:44,366
The baby chicks are hatching.

185
00:08:44,433 --> 00:08:46,233
[peeping]

186
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:48,500
[in unison] Aww. Baby chicks.

187
00:08:49,466 --> 00:08:53,600
[Granny Pig] Now the chicks have hatched,
it really is springtime.

188
00:08:54,633 --> 00:08:57,233
Let's pretend to be baby chicks.

189
00:08:57,466 --> 00:08:59,466
[imitating baby chickens]

190
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:03,800
♪ I'm a little chick
Singing cheep, cheep, cheep ♪

191
00:09:04,033 --> 00:09:07,666
♪ I like to pick up food
With my beak, beak, beak ♪

192
00:09:07,733 --> 00:09:11,400
♪ I've a fluffy yellow head
Some straw for my bed ♪

193
00:09:11,466 --> 00:09:15,199
♪ And I jump up and down
Singing cheep, cheep, cheep ♪

194
00:09:15,266 --> 00:09:16,400
[giggling]

195
00:09:18,699 --> 00:09:21,733
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

196
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:25,000
[narrator] Peppa and her family have come
to the summer fete.

197
00:09:25,066 --> 00:09:26,266
[Peppa and George giggle]

198
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:30,000
[grunts] Look, a display
of rescue vehicles.

199
00:09:30,066 --> 00:09:32,666
Granddad Dog is showing his pickup truck.

200
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:36,300
[woofs] This is the sound
my pickup truck makes.

201
00:09:36,366 --> 00:09:37,633
[horn blares]

202
00:09:37,699 --> 00:09:40,466
Mommy Sheep is showing the fire engine.

203
00:09:40,533 --> 00:09:43,733
[bleats] This is the sound
the fire engine makes.

204
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,333
[siren sounds]

205
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:48,400
And Miss Rabbit
is showing her rescue helicopter.

206
00:09:48,466 --> 00:09:51,533
This is the sound my helicopter makes.

207
00:09:52,033 --> 00:09:53,800
-[beeping]
-[voice] Helicopter reversing.

208
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:55,733
Helicopter reversing.

209
00:09:56,699 --> 00:09:58,566
Would you like to go for a ride?

210
00:09:58,633 --> 00:10:00,000
-Yes, please.
-[giggles]

211
00:10:00,066 --> 00:10:01,800
Okay, hop in.

212
00:10:03,066 --> 00:10:08,333
Oh, dear. There's no room for me.
Never mind. I'll watch from the ground.

213
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,400
Daddy Pig doesn't like heights.

214
00:10:11,699 --> 00:10:14,300
Whee-hee! We're going up in the air.

215
00:10:14,366 --> 00:10:17,500
-[grunts]
-Yes. It can go straight up.

216
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:19,566
Up!

217
00:10:20,133 --> 00:10:22,100
It can go straight down.

218
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:23,633
[Peppa and George] Whee!

219
00:10:25,066 --> 00:10:26,733
It can even loop the loop.

220
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[Peppa giggling]

221
00:10:30,533 --> 00:10:33,300
Poor Daddy. He's missing all the fun.

222
00:10:33,366 --> 00:10:35,500
Yes, poor Daddy.

223
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:37,633
One ice cream, please.

224
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,466
Mm. That's nice.

225
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,766
Maybe we should land now.

226
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,766
[man on speaker] Emergency. Emergency.

227
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Calling rescue helicopter.

228
00:10:48,066 --> 00:10:49,266
I'm on my way.

229
00:10:49,333 --> 00:10:52,333
You're in luck. We've got a job to do.

230
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,699
Mr. Bull is digging up the road.

231
00:10:55,266 --> 00:10:58,466
Moo. Hello, Miss Rabbit.

232
00:10:59,199 --> 00:11:03,000
I've got a big metal pipe
that needs lifting.

233
00:11:03,066 --> 00:11:04,699
Okay, Mr. Bull.

234
00:11:04,766 --> 00:11:07,466
How can you lift that big pipe?

235
00:11:07,533 --> 00:11:09,666
With my big magnet.

236
00:11:13,166 --> 00:11:14,100
[Peppa] Hooray!

237
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:18,133
What are you going to do with the pipe?

238
00:11:18,199 --> 00:11:21,266
Um... I'm not really sure.

239
00:11:21,733 --> 00:11:26,500
I know. I'll put it down here,
where someone can easily find it.

240
00:11:28,033 --> 00:11:30,233
Now I can give you a lift home.

241
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,066
But what about Daddy?

242
00:11:32,466 --> 00:11:34,333
[keypad beeps]

243
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,000
[phone ringing]

244
00:11:36,066 --> 00:11:37,666
-Hello?
-[Mommy Pig] Daddy Pig,

245
00:11:37,733 --> 00:11:41,633
can you make your own way home?
Miss Rabbit is giving us a lift.

246
00:11:41,699 --> 00:11:42,666
Okay.

247
00:11:42,733 --> 00:11:44,300
[Peppa] Daddy, Daddy.

248
00:11:44,366 --> 00:11:48,300
We went up and down, and round and round.

249
00:11:48,366 --> 00:11:51,466
Ho, ho. I'm really sad
to have missed that.

250
00:11:51,533 --> 00:11:52,800
See you back at home.

251
00:11:56,533 --> 00:11:57,433
[tires screech]

252
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,500
Who put that pipe there?

253
00:12:01,066 --> 00:12:03,633
I know. I'll take a shortcut.

254
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,133
Hmm. It's a bit muddy.

255
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,266
[engine sputters]

256
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:13,733
Come on, car. Daddy Pig needs to get home.

257
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,366
[engine revs]

258
00:12:15,433 --> 00:12:17,533
Daddy Pig is stuck.

259
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:20,500
I'll ring for Granddad Dog's pickup truck.

260
00:12:20,566 --> 00:12:22,466
[keypad beeps]

261
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:24,166
[phone rings]

262
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:27,199
[woofs] Hello. Breakdown recovery.

263
00:12:27,266 --> 00:12:28,500
I'm stuck in the mud.

264
00:12:28,566 --> 00:12:32,000
-Can you come and rescue me, please?
-Sorry, Daddy Pig,

265
00:12:32,066 --> 00:12:37,166
I'm moving a big metal pipe
that some maniac has left in the road.

266
00:12:37,233 --> 00:12:40,500
I'll pass you on
to the next rescue service.

267
00:12:40,566 --> 00:12:42,266
[phone rings]

268
00:12:42,333 --> 00:12:44,300
Hello. Fire service.

269
00:12:44,366 --> 00:12:47,266
[Daddy Pig] I'm stuck in the mud.
Can you rescue me, please?

270
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:48,433
Sorry Daddy Pig,

271
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,633
I'm rescuing a tortoise
that's stuck up a tree.

272
00:12:51,699 --> 00:12:53,633
Come down, Tiddles.

273
00:12:53,699 --> 00:12:58,633
I don't know why you like climbing trees.
You're a tortoise.

274
00:12:58,699 --> 00:13:00,699
[bleats] Don't worry, Daddy Pig,

275
00:13:00,766 --> 00:13:04,433
I'll pass you on
to the highest rescue service in the land.

276
00:13:05,533 --> 00:13:06,533
[helicopter whirring]

277
00:13:07,733 --> 00:13:09,133
What's that noise?

278
00:13:09,599 --> 00:13:11,333
Whoa!

279
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:13,400
I'm flying.

280
00:13:13,466 --> 00:13:16,300
Miss Rabbit's helicopter
has rescued Daddy Pig.

281
00:13:16,366 --> 00:13:17,633
Hooray!

282
00:13:17,699 --> 00:13:22,133
Lucky Daddy gets a helicopter ride
after all.

283
00:13:22,533 --> 00:13:25,233
Shall we show him
what my helicopter can do?

284
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,300
-[Peppa] Yes.
-[Mommy Pig] Yes.

285
00:13:26,366 --> 00:13:28,366
It can go straight up.

286
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:29,533
Whoa!

287
00:13:30,099 --> 00:13:32,300
It can go straight down.

288
00:13:32,733 --> 00:13:34,033
Whoa!

289
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:37,199
It can even loop the loop.

290
00:13:37,266 --> 00:13:38,800
[groaning]

291
00:13:40,333 --> 00:13:44,133
Everyone likes going up and down
and round and round

292
00:13:44,199 --> 00:13:46,666
in Miss Rabbit's helicopter.

293
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,433
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

294
00:13:53,699 --> 00:13:57,233
[narrator] Peppa and George's cousins
are coming to visit today.

295
00:13:57,599 --> 00:14:01,400
Mommy,
how long before Cousin Chloë is here?

296
00:14:01,466 --> 00:14:05,199
Not long now, Peppa.
Baby Alexander is coming, too, remember?

297
00:14:05,266 --> 00:14:10,066
Oh, babies cry all the time.
They're so noisy.

298
00:14:10,133 --> 00:14:13,699
I'm sure Baby Alexander
won't be that noisy.

299
00:14:14,033 --> 00:14:14,766
[crying]

300
00:14:16,266 --> 00:14:17,633
What's that sound?

301
00:14:17,699 --> 00:14:19,400
Is it a car alarm?

302
00:14:19,466 --> 00:14:21,466
Is it a fire engine?

303
00:14:22,133 --> 00:14:24,400
No, it's Baby Alexander.

304
00:14:24,466 --> 00:14:26,233
[crying continues]

305
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:29,166
Hello, Peppa. Hello, George.

306
00:14:29,233 --> 00:14:30,800
Hello, Cousin Chloë.

307
00:14:31,033 --> 00:14:32,599
Hello, everyone.

308
00:14:32,666 --> 00:14:34,300
Hello, Uncle Pig.

309
00:14:34,366 --> 00:14:35,233
Hello.

310
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,666
Hello, Aunty Pig.

311
00:14:36,733 --> 00:14:40,133
You remember Baby Alexander,
don't you, Peppa?

312
00:14:40,199 --> 00:14:41,166
Yes.

313
00:14:42,166 --> 00:14:45,333
-[music playing]
-[Alexander giggling]

314
00:14:46,033 --> 00:14:48,066
Are you staying for a few days?

315
00:14:48,133 --> 00:14:52,266
No, this is what Alexander needs
for just one day.

316
00:14:52,333 --> 00:14:56,033
Can't go anywhere
without all these baby things.

317
00:14:56,099 --> 00:14:58,699
-Oh.
-Hello, Baby Alexander.

318
00:14:58,766 --> 00:15:00,800
He can't talk, Peppa.

319
00:15:01,033 --> 00:15:05,000
If he can't talk, then how do you
know what he wants?

320
00:15:05,066 --> 00:15:06,333
We guess.

321
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,633
[cries]

322
00:15:07,699 --> 00:15:10,166
I'm guessing he's hungry.

323
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:13,633
Peppa, would you like
to help feed Alexander?

324
00:15:13,699 --> 00:15:15,433
Yes, please.

325
00:15:17,033 --> 00:15:19,366
It is lunchtime for Baby Alexander.

326
00:15:19,433 --> 00:15:23,566
Cousin Peppa is going to feed you today,
Alexander.

327
00:15:23,633 --> 00:15:25,633
Here you are, baby.

328
00:15:25,699 --> 00:15:27,266
-[groans]
-Oh.

329
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:29,166
Here it is.

330
00:15:29,233 --> 00:15:30,433
-[groans]
-[scoffs]

331
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:33,033
-He keeps turning his head.
-[groans]

332
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:36,300
Feeding Baby Alexander is quite hard.

333
00:15:36,366 --> 00:15:37,500
Watch this.

334
00:15:37,566 --> 00:15:40,233
Here comes the airplane.

335
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:42,166
[makes whooping sound]

336
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:43,166
[laughs]

337
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:47,599
Alexander likes it if you pretend
the spoon is an airplane.

338
00:15:47,666 --> 00:15:49,199
You have a go, Peppa.

339
00:15:49,266 --> 00:15:51,633
[grunts] Here comes the airplane.

340
00:15:51,699 --> 00:15:53,199
[makes babbling sound]

341
00:15:53,266 --> 00:15:56,300
Open your mouth, and in through the doors.

342
00:15:56,466 --> 00:15:57,766
Whoosh!

343
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,166
-Hooray!
-Hooray!

344
00:15:59,233 --> 00:16:01,733
[giggles] That was an airplane.

345
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:05,099
Can you say "airplane"?

346
00:16:05,166 --> 00:16:07,766
I told you, he can't talk.

347
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,800
He hasn't even said his first word yet.

348
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:14,566
Peppa, do you remember
what your first word was?

349
00:16:14,633 --> 00:16:17,333
-No.
-It was "mommy."

350
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:20,666
[grunts] I thought Peppa's first word
was "daddy."

351
00:16:20,733 --> 00:16:22,000
No, "mommy."

352
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:25,366
What was George's first word?

353
00:16:25,433 --> 00:16:26,800
Dinosaur.

354
00:16:27,033 --> 00:16:29,633
George's first word was "dinosaur."

355
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:33,133
Somebody looks like they had a good lunch.

356
00:16:33,199 --> 00:16:34,066
Yes.

357
00:16:34,133 --> 00:16:35,533
Bath time I think.

358
00:16:37,233 --> 00:16:39,633
Baby Alexander is having a bath.

359
00:16:39,699 --> 00:16:41,166
[giggles]

360
00:16:41,699 --> 00:16:46,633
This is Mr. Dinosaur.
Can you say "dinosaur"?

361
00:16:46,699 --> 00:16:48,233
[babbles]

362
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,699
He can't talk, Peppa.

363
00:16:50,766 --> 00:16:53,533
[grunts] But he will talk one day.

364
00:16:53,599 --> 00:16:56,099
Then you'll know what he wants.

365
00:16:56,166 --> 00:16:59,166
What do you want to do now, Alexander?

366
00:16:59,233 --> 00:17:00,666
[babbles]

367
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:04,200
[grunts] I think he wants
to go for a walk.

368
00:17:04,266 --> 00:17:08,000
He can't walk yet,
but he can go out in his buggy.

369
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,500
[grunts] That's a clever little buggy.

370
00:17:13,566 --> 00:17:17,700
Yes. Five gears, mud guards,
and ABS as standard.

371
00:17:17,766 --> 00:17:19,666
Blah, blah, blah.

372
00:17:19,733 --> 00:17:21,700
That's how daddies talk.

373
00:17:21,766 --> 00:17:25,300
-[coos]
-Alexander likes it when you talk, Peppa.

374
00:17:25,366 --> 00:17:28,766
That's because I am very interesting.

375
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,466
[laughing]

376
00:17:30,533 --> 00:17:34,633
This is the sky. Can you say "sky"?

377
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,133
[babbles]

378
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:41,066
The sky is where rain comes from.
Can you say "rain"?

379
00:17:41,133 --> 00:17:42,066
[giggles]

380
00:17:42,133 --> 00:17:45,133
Rain is good for ducks and plants,

381
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:48,600
and making muddy puddles.

382
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:51,366
Peppa has found a big muddy puddle.

383
00:17:51,433 --> 00:17:56,733
[grunts] Look, Alexander,
I'm jumping up and down in a puddle.

384
00:17:57,066 --> 00:17:58,000
[giggles]

385
00:17:58,066 --> 00:17:59,166
[giggling]

386
00:17:59,233 --> 00:18:02,466
[grunts] I love jumping
up and down in puddles.

387
00:18:02,533 --> 00:18:03,766
Puddles.

388
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,133
[all] Ooh!

389
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:08,399
Alexander has said his first word.
Puddles.

390
00:18:08,466 --> 00:18:11,166
[in unison] Hooray! Puddles!

391
00:18:11,233 --> 00:18:14,233
And I taught him to say it.

392
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:15,766
Puddles.

393
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[laughing]

394
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,300
[theme song playing]

